  "body": "Command payloads containing duplicate JSON fields previously collapsed to the last value before the daemon could reject the ambiguity. The command endpoint now uses the existing recursive strict JSON visitor through Axum's JSON extractor, then validates the closed command envelope before entering the ledger transaction. Content-type, body-size and authentication error protections remain in place.\n\nA real local HTTP regression covers duplicate root, nested and escaped-equivalent keys, unknown envelope fields and trailing data. Each refusal preserves command, event and outbox state; a subsequent valid request can use the same key and replay its original result.\n\nValidation on b1cf8f3df68931a85a2f2b3e495deebeb458edb1: ten focused HTTP tests and strict all-target Clippy passed. The full inventory check passed with 1,238 identities: 1,192 standalone plus unchanged 34 contract, 3 egress and 9 family. Independent static review verified source, the one-test addition and unchanged required checks. Full local required passed, including all 1,192 standalone tests, 34 contract tests, lint, security and docs. Push run 34434537685 and PR run 34434592659 passed all seven required checks each on this exact head.\n\nThis is command admission hardening. Task-shaped server allocations, scheduling and native lifecycle remain open; no live provider or release admission is claimed.\n",
